✅ ✅ 1. What is CI/CD ?
👉 Definition:
CI/CD is a process to automate code integration, testing, and deployment

✅ CI (Continuous Integration)

Developers push code frequently ✅
Build + test automatically ✅


✅ CD (Continuous Delivery / Deployment)

Automatically deploy code ✅
Faster and reliable releases ✅


✅ ✅ 2. What is Jenkins ?
👉 Definition:
Jenkins is an automation server used to implement CI/CD pipelines

✅ Key Points:

Open-source ✅
Plugin-based ✅
Supports pipeline as code ✅
Integrates with Git, Docker, Kubernetes ✅


✅ 3. Jenkins Architecture
👉 Components:
Master (Controller)
→ manages jobs, schedules builds

Agent (Node)
→ executes jobs

Executor
→ runs builds

Plugins
→ extend functionality



👉 Flow:
Developer → Git Push → Jenkins → Build → Test → Deploy


✅ ✅ 4. Types of Jenkins Jobs

Freestyle Job ✅
Pipeline Job ✅ (most important)
Multibranch Pipeline ✅


✅ ✅ 5. What is Jenkins Pipeline ?
👉 Pipeline is a set of steps defined in code (Jenkinsfile)

✅ Types:

Declarative ✅ (recommended)
Scripted ✅


6. Explain all parameters which can be used in jenkins pipeline.

string            # Used to pass single-line text input (app name, version, URL)

choice            # Used to select one value from predefined list (env: dev/test/prod)

booleanParam      # Used for true/false option (enable/disable deploy, feature flag)

text              # Used for multi-line input (config, JSON, YAML data)

password          # Used to pass sensitive value (masked in UI, not recommended for prod)

file              # Used to upload a file during build (cert, config, script)

credentials       # Used to securely pass secrets like API keys, SSH keys (best practice)

run               # Used to select a build from another job (job dependency)


parameters {
    string(name: 'APP_NAME', defaultValue: 'myapp', description: 'Application name')

    choice(name: 'ENV', choices: ['dev', 'test', 'prod'], description: 'Select environment')

    booleanParam(name: 'DEPLOY', defaultValue: true, description: 'Enable deployment')

    credentials(name: 'CREDS_ID', description: 'Select Jenkins credentials (SSH/API key)')
}
``
